cf-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use nativegate, please cite it using the
  metadata of the Zenodo record linked below, or this citation.
title: nativegate: make legacy C++/C/Fortran AI-ready and microservice-ready
authors:
  - given-names: Abdul
    family-names: Rabiu
    email: sr.rabiu@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://github.com/ravikings'
version: 0.1.9
date-released: '2026-09-23'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ravikings/nativegate'
url: 'https://nativegate.dev'
abstract: >-
  A code generator for the C++/Fortran-to-Python boundary: from an
  unmodified legacy deck or header it produces f2py/pybind11 bindings,
  a CMake build, an installable wheel, tests, a FastAPI service,
  Docker/Kubernetes artifacts, and a numerical golden-record
  regression harness that pins the compiled code's return values.
keywords:
  - fortran
  - legacy-code
  - python-bindings
  - mcp
  - scientific-computing
  - modernization
identifiers:
  - description: 'Concept DOI, covers all released versions'
    type: doi
    value: '10.5281/zenodo.22929352'
